===Etymology 2===
The mainstream opinion on this word is that it comes from old uses of the stem {{m|lv|balts||white}} ([[q.v.]]) in names of places containing water, giving rise to the name of the Baltic Sea (already {{cog|la|Mare Balticum}}); it is possible that {{m|ine-bsl-pro|*balt-}} in {{etyl|prg|-}} placenames referred originally to the sea or coastal area. Another suggestion is that {{cog|la|Mare Balticum}} is to be derived from {{etyl|non|lv}} {{m|non|balti}}, {{cog|da|balte}}, from {{etyl|la|lv}} {{m|la|balteum||belt}} (whence {{cog|de|Belt||sea strait}}), perhaps because of this sea's narrowness, or because of the many islands and straits between islands and the continent.<ref name="LEV">{{R:lv:LEV}}</ref>

